{"id": "EUVD-2026-102489", "enisaUuid": "deab5424-f1a9-3ab2-8497-9c8b285b84f2", "description": "Trudesk through 1.2.11 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability that allows any authenticated user to read private conversations by supplying another conversation's id. Attackers can request GET /api/v1/messages/conversation/:id, which lacks participant checks, to obtain full message history plus participants' usernames, full names and email addresses.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:08:37", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/trudesk-conversation-messages-idor", "https://github.com/polonel/trudesk/blob/v1.2.11/src/controllers/api/v1/messages.js#L255-L308", "https://github.com/polonel/trudesk/blob/v1.2.11/src/models/chat/message.js#L70-L101", "https://github.com/polonel/trudesk", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/trudesk-through-1.2.11-authorization-bypass-via-get-api-v1-messages-conversation-id"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111345", "GHSA-xm42-mhff-286m"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f43b2971-5121-32ec-bf38-5bc1aafedac1", "product": {"name": "trudesk", "vendor": {"name": "polonel"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.2.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a0ff2eb3-8135-3e7c-82e3-2a0a054dac90", "vendor": {"name": "polonel"}}], "isExploited": false}